.TH ROCKLAKE 1 "September 2026" "RockLake 0.63.1" "RockLake Manual"
.SH NAME
rocklake \- DuckLake catalog service and operator CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rocklake
.I COMMAND
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
RockLake provides a bounded PostgreSQL wire surface for a DuckLake 1.0
catalog backed by SlateDB and object storage.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B serve
Start the PostgreSQL wire server.
.TP
.B doctor
Run a read-only startup preflight.
.TP
.B status
Check catalog readiness and version domains.
.TP
.B support bundle
Write a redacted support bundle to a new directory.
.TP
.B capacity report
Report measured capacity and projected cost.
.TP
.B catalog, catalogs, registry
Manage catalog data, routes, and the managed registry.
.TP
.B config
Validate or print configuration.
.TP
.B completions
Generate Bash, Zsh, or Fish completion scripts.
.SH SUPPORT BUNDLES
.EX
rocklake support bundle --catalog ./lake --output ./rocklake-support
.EE
The bundle includes version, redacted configuration, status, verification, and
optional Prometheus metrics. The output directory must not already exist.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./rocklake.toml
Default configuration file when present.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rocklake (1)
.SH SECURITY
Do not attach a support bundle without reviewing deployment-specific paths and
identifiers. Credentials, encryption keys, and catalog URL userinfo are
redacted by the command.
